    "m2_prompt_trader_proposal_original": "**Action**: Hold\n\n**Reasoning**: The investment plan calls for maintaining the current AAPL position at ~$180.34 given the balanced bull/bear case. The fundamentals are solid ($39.9B quarterly operating cash flow, 1.27x asset coverage, $30.6B returned to shareholders), but the technical picture is deteriorating\u2014four consecutive down closes, price below all key moving averages including the 200-day SMA at $181.03, and MACD histogram expanding 12x in a week. With RSI at 37 (not yet oversold) and the only nearby support at the lower Bollinger Band ($178.88), the risk-reward is roughly balanced. The prudent stance is to hold and wait for either a reclaim of the 200-day SMA (bull validation) or a break below the lower band (bear validation).\n\n**Entry Price**: 180.34\n\n**Stop Loss**: 178.88\n\n**Position Sizing**: No more than 3-4% of portfolio; consider trimming up to 25-30% into strength toward the 10-day EMA at $183.69\n\nFINAL TRANSACTION PROPOSAL: **HOLD**",
